## AgentForge Lean Routing

Use the `lean-routing` skill for cost-aware engineering work.

- Execute one trivial deterministic operation directly rather than spawning an agent.
- Delegate repeated/read-heavy/high-volume low-judgment work to `cheap-ops`.
- Delegate tiny exact edits to `cheap-edit`.
- Delegate small pattern-following implementation to `cheap-coder`.
- Use `reviewer` or the parent for interpretation and risk analysis.
- Keep architecture, ambiguity, security, migrations, concurrency, and cross-cutting decisions in the parent.
- Cheap workers return `ESCALATE` rather than guess.
- Prefer deterministic verification after edits.
<!-- agentforge:lean-routing:end -->
